Status and evidence for the exchange lemma

Remark 4.5. All steps of this document except Lemma 4.4 are complete proofs from (H1)–(H4).
For Lemma 4.4 we provide:
(a) exhaustive finite verification (Proposition 4.6): in 154 quotient hyperfields and the sign hyperfield every one of the 618 867 test configurations with δ ≥ 1 admits a descent, and every
one of the 137 403 free instances satisfies the conclusion of Theorem 2.1;
(b) the mechanism: the only obstruction to replacing a bad value p ̸= −w by −w is a required
pair sum being a singleton, and Lemma 4.3 shows that singletons among the degree-two cells
propagate down to a level-1 collapse, excluded by (F); the hard residual situation is a pair
{p1 , p2 } of bad values none of whose mates q ∈ pi ⊞ (−w) lies in P ;
(c) cube-level structure (Section 5): modulo cubes the six target terms have classes {0, 0, 0, w̄, w̄, w̄}
with 3w̄ = 0, and no pair among the six terms is ever a singleton in any verified instance,
consistent with the descent never being blocked by a level-2 singleton.
The missing piece for a fully self-contained proof is a uniform axiomatic argument for the residual
situation in (b). With this caveat, Theorem 2.1 is stated as the correct answer, with the single
dependence on Lemma 4.4 made explicit rather than hidden.
